Package: wavscatengine
Title: Rust Engine for 'wavscat': Bit-Identical Scattering Features
Version: 0.1.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Aidan", "D. Bindoff", email = "aidan.bindoff@utas.edu.au",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Kymatio developers", role = "cph",
           comment = "Filter bank and cascade design, BSD-3-Clause"))
Description: The compiled engine behind 'wavscat'. It computes wavelet
    scattering and joint time-frequency scattering with the same Rust core
    used from Python and in the browser, so features are bit-for-bit
    identical across languages and platforms. 'wavscat' uses this package automatically when it is installed and
    falls back to its own pure R engine otherwise.
License: BSD_3_clause + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
SystemRequirements: Cargo (Rust's package manager), rustc >= 1.77
Depends:
    R (>= 4.1)
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
URL: https://github.com/ABindoff/wavscat-core
BugReports: https://github.com/ABindoff/wavscat-core/issues
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.0.0
